===Season format===
The regular season runs from the first weekend of September through the second weekend of December. Each Division 1 team plays a 14-game schedule, facing each division opponent at least once along with select cross-division and rivalry matchups. The top four teams in Division 1 qualify for the playoffs.

The postseason is conducted through two single-elimination rounds. In the semifinals, the first-seeded team hosts the fourth seed while the second seed hosts the third seed. The two winners advance to the [[Rice Bowl]], the national championship game held on the second Saturday of January at a rotating neutral site such as the Toyozawa Dome, Okami National Stadium, or the Aizawa Maritime Arena.

===Game regulations and tactical profile===
The X-League operates under canonical [[Lurandian Football]] rules as codified by the [[Lurandian Football Union]] (LFU), emphasizing sustained tempo, physical endurance, and disciplined line play. Regulation matches are contested across three 20-minute periods designated as Thirds, totaling 60 minutes of playing time with a 20-second play clock between downs. In the final three minutes of the third period, the Dead-Time Clock Rule takes effect, stopping the match clock on all official whistles until the ball is centered on the subsequent snap.

Offenses operate under the Three-and-Twelve system, requiring teams to gain 12 yards within three downs rather than four. To balance offensive momentum, any team gaining nine or more yards across its first two attempts is awarded a Breakthrough Fourth Down. The line of scrimmage is structured around a mandatory 1.5-yard (4.5-foot) Neutral Corridor that separates offensive and defensive lines before the snap. Offensive and defensive linemen are required to align in upright or semi-crouched stances, while cut-blocking and chop-blocking below the waist are strictly outlawed to emphasize upper-body leverage and drive blocking.

Under the league's Two-Way Anchors mandate, each active roster must designate two players who play both offensive and defensive series during each 20-minute Third. Tactical schemes frequently exploit the Dual Forward Release provision, which permits two separate forward passes behind the line of scrimmage on a single play, alongside the Protected Lateral Rule, which rules any uncontested dropped backward pitch dead at the spot of contact rather than treating it as a live fumble.

The league employs a multi-tiered scoring matrix centered on the standard 6-point touchdown. Following a touchdown, teams choose between a 1-point conversion kick from the 15-yard line, a 2-point scrimmage run or pass from the 3-yard line, a 2-point drop-kick from the 25-yard line, or a high-risk 3-point High Conversion scrimmage play from the 10-yard line. Field goals struck inside the 45-yard line yield 3 points, whereas long-range Cannon Goals converted from 45 yards or greater and open-play drop-kicks earn 4 points. Defensive units can also register points through the standard 2-point safety, the single-point [[Rouge (Lurandian Football)|rouge]] awarded when kicking into the end zone, and the 1-point Iron Stop awarded when a defense successfully turns over an opponent inside the 5-yard line on downs. Kicking plays require a mandatory 5-yard safety halo in lieu of a fair catch, and return units are legally permitted to execute Return Punts back downfield, while kicking-team players who align behind the punter at the snap may act as onside chasers to recover loose balls.

===Foreign player regulations===
The X-League permits each team to roster a maximum of four foreign (non-Sanese) players, with no more than two on the field simultaneously. The majority of foreign players come from [[Kaneda]] and [[Kazabune]], where Lurandian Football is the dominant gridiron code. The league also maintains a "Shendan exception" allowing one additional player from a [[Shendan Ocean]] nation without counting against the foreign quota, reflecting Okaiken's regional sporting ties.

